BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:trainingos-v4-push_chest-2026-10-05@trainingos.local
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20261005T110000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20261005T123000
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;INTERVAL=6;COUNT=8
SUMMARY:TrainingOS V4 - Push / Chest
LOCATION:Gunyama Park Aquatic and Recreation Centre
DESCRIPTION:Primary target: Chest\nOverlap rule: Keep shoulder and triceps 
 accessory volume limited.\nFocus: PR-aware chest work\; load and set count
  finalized from morning recovery.\nMorning inputs: sleep\, HRV\, Body Batt
 ery\, readiness\, recent PR state.\nLoad: dynamic\; do not copy a fixed we
 ight from the calendar.\nRecord: sets\, reps\, weight\, RPE\, pain\, and t
 echnique notes in Garmin/TrainingOS.\nFallback: If recovery is poor: reduc
 e volume or use technique work\; do not force a PR.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT45M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:TrainingOS V4 - Push / Chest
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:trainingos-v4-core_a-2026-10-05@trainingos.local
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20261006T110000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20261006T120000
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;INTERVAL=6;COUNT=8
SUMMARY:TrainingOS V4 - Core A
LOCATION:Gunyama Park Aquatic and Recreation Centre
DESCRIPTION:Primary target: Core\nOverlap rule: Avoid grip-heavy\, hanging\
 , and high-volume hip-flexor work before legs.\nFocus: Medium/high-intensi
 ty trunk flexion and anti-extension with controlled fatigue.\nMorning inpu
 ts: sleep\, HRV\, Body Battery\, readiness\, recent PR state.\nLoad: dynam
 ic\; do not copy a fixed weight from the calendar.\nRecord: sets\, reps\, 
 weight\, RPE\, pain\, and technique notes in Garmin/TrainingOS.\nFallback:
  If bracing is fatigued: use low-load control work or recovery only.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT45M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:TrainingOS V4 - Core A
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:trainingos-v4-legs-2026-10-05@trainingos.local
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20261007T110000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20261007T123000
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;INTERVAL=6;COUNT=8
SUMMARY:TrainingOS V4 - Legs
LOCATION:Gunyama Park Aquatic and Recreation Centre
DESCRIPTION:Primary target: Legs\nOverlap rule: No upper-body loading\; pro
 tect the prior pressing chain.\nFocus: One lower-body priority with PR-awa
 re progression and an RPE cap.\nMorning inputs: sleep\, HRV\, Body Battery
 \, readiness\, recent PR state.\nLoad: dynamic\; do not copy a fixed weigh
 t from the calendar.\nRecord: sets\, reps\, weight\, RPE\, pain\, and tech
 nique notes in Garmin/TrainingOS.\nFallback: If recovery is poor: remove o
 ne accessory block and cap all work at RPE 7.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT45M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:TrainingOS V4 - Legs
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:trainingos-v4-core_b-2026-10-05@trainingos.local
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20261008T110000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20261008T120000
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;INTERVAL=6;COUNT=8
SUMMARY:TrainingOS V4 - Core B
LOCATION:Gunyama Park Aquatic and Recreation Centre
DESCRIPTION:Primary target: Core\nOverlap rule: Avoid hanging\, grip-heavy\
 , and lower-back-fatiguing work before pull.\nFocus: Medium/high-intensity
  trunk work that preserves grip and spinal erectors.\nMorning inputs: slee
 p\, HRV\, Body Battery\, readiness\, recent PR state.\nLoad: dynamic\; do 
 not copy a fixed weight from the calendar.\nRecord: sets\, reps\, weight\,
  RPE\, pain\, and technique notes in Garmin/TrainingOS.\nFallback: If legs
  or lower back remain fatigued: use supported control work or rest.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT45M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:TrainingOS V4 - Core B
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:trainingos-v4-pull_back-2026-10-05@trainingos.local
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20261009T110000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20261009T123000
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;INTERVAL=6;COUNT=8
SUMMARY:TrainingOS V4 - Pull / Back
LOCATION:Gunyama Park Aquatic and Recreation Centre
DESCRIPTION:Primary target: Back\nOverlap rule: Biceps are secondary\; avoi
 d turning the session into an arm-priority day.\nFocus: Back-priority vert
 ical and horizontal pulling with conservative arm volume.\nMorning inputs:
  sleep\, HRV\, Body Battery\, readiness\, recent PR state.\nLoad: dynamic\
 ; do not copy a fixed weight from the calendar.\nRecord: sets\, reps\, wei
 ght\, RPE\, pain\, and technique notes in Garmin/TrainingOS.\nFallback: If
  recovery is poor: reduce one row/curl block and keep two reps in reserve.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT45M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:TrainingOS V4 - Pull / Back
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:trainingos-v4-recovery_sync-2026-10-05@trainingos.local
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20261010T110000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20261010T113000
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;INTERVAL=6;COUNT=8
SUMMARY:TrainingOS V4 - Recovery / Sync
LOCATION:Gunyama Park Aquatic and Recreation Centre
DESCRIPTION:Primary target: Recovery\nOverlap rule: No primary resistance-t
 raining target.\nFocus: Sync Garmin data\, correct the prior sessions\, an
 d review the next cycle.\nMorning inputs: sleep\, HRV\, Body Battery\, rea
 diness\, recent PR state.\nLoad: dynamic\; do not copy a fixed weight from
  the calendar.\nRecord: sets\, reps\, weight\, RPE\, pain\, and technique 
 notes in Garmin/TrainingOS.\nFallback: If data quality is incomplete: keep
  the next plan as draft and do not auto-push.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT45M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:TrainingOS V4 - Recovery / Sync
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
